WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.450
Okay.

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:04.120
This is sort of funny and it's also very,
very depressing.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:08.420
At a recent fundraiser, Democratic candidate
and former Barack Obama, vice president Joe

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:15.480
Biden made some promises to wealthy donors,
including that he won't quote demonize them

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:20.130
and that nothing big will change for them
if he becomes president of the United States.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.370
And my reaction was, yeah, Joe, we know that.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:23.640
I don't think you had to say that.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.890
We know that Joe Biden basically saying the
quiet part out loud, making clear that his

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:34.560
politics are politics of centrist, status
quo, uh, center leftism and we knew that right

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:39.780
here is a list of what Joe Biden had to say
just a couple of days ago.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:42.550
To a group of rich donors in New York City.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:45.940
Joe Biden told them, I need you very badly.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:51.740
Joe Biden told these wealthy contributors
in New York City, no one standard of living

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.420
will change.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.470
Nothing would fundamentally change.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:01:01.310
Joe Biden said that rich people are quote,
just as patriotic, as poor people.

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:06.790
Joe Biden said, quote, we may not want to
demonize anybody who has made money.

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:11.189
And Joe Biden said, I hope if I win this nomination,
I won't let you down.

00:01:11.189 --> 00:01:14.090
Meaning you rich people who are giving me
money.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:17.140
We know Joe, we know this is, this is actually
great.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:18.140
In a sense.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:21.770
This is confirmation about exactly what we
will get with Joe Biden.

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:28.340
We knew that Joe Biden was the status quo
economic policy would some slight leftward

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:33.009
moves combined with moderately left social
policy.

00:01:33.009 --> 00:01:35.069
That's what we could expect from Joe Biden.

00:01:35.069 --> 00:01:36.420
And he's confirming it here.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:39.509
This idea of nothing will fundamentally change.

00:01:39.509 --> 00:01:41.060
That's literally status quo.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:45.850
Centrism it's, I'm basically in the middle
and slightly to the left on, on social policy.

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:51.310
Uh, and I'll make some tweaks on economic
policy, but nothing is substantively substantively

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:52.549
going to change.

00:01:52.549 --> 00:01:54.329
He needs the rich donors.

00:01:54.329 --> 00:01:57.789
He's not going to do anything that's going
to be scary to them and he's telling them,

00:01:57.789 --> 00:01:59.219
I'm safe for you.

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:06.189
I will say stuff on the campaign trail about
economic justice and inequality and paying

00:02:06.189 --> 00:02:08.849
of people's fair share and all of this stuff.

00:02:08.849 --> 00:02:12.930
But that big picture, he'll work around the
edges and he's not going to substantively

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:14.549
change things for them.

00:02:14.549 --> 00:02:16.790
Uh, other than playing in the margins a little
bit.

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:19.780
So this is the exact opposite of change.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:20.780
You can believe in.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:26.390
It's no change and you can be sure of it and
you can safely vote for me without worrying

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:28.120
that I'm going to take too much of your money.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:33.810
He's saying there will be some cake crumbs
for the middle class and the poor sprinkled

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:40.400
on them, but that big picture, the rich are
going to keep their full rich decadent black

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:44.340
forest chocolate cakes or whatever analogy
or metaphor you want to apply here.

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:49.720
This is like a really memorable non story
of the campaign in the sense that we knew

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:53.159
that this was why Joe Biden was the safe establishment
candidate.

00:02:53.159 --> 00:02:57.739
He will say mostly the right things in public
on policy.

00:02:57.739 --> 00:03:02.860
Now he has gaffes obviously, uh, but he is
going to be completely predictable in his

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:03.860
governance.

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:06.209
There is not going to be anything earth shaking
that will happen.

00:03:06.209 --> 00:03:11.379
And in a sense this is very similar to what
we expected with Hillary Clinton when I've

00:03:11.379 --> 00:03:16.019
said that a Hillary Clinton presidency would
have been boring in a sense.

00:03:16.019 --> 00:03:18.340
It's because she would've been predictably
center left.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:23.909
We would have as a progressive show critiqued
her from further to her left.

00:03:23.909 --> 00:03:28.819
She wouldn't have done anything that would
have generated the worldwide cartoonish embarrassment

00:03:28.819 --> 00:03:30.959
that Donald Trump has generated.

00:03:30.959 --> 00:03:32.739
But it would have been all of the expected
stuff.

00:03:32.739 --> 00:03:36.150
There would've been some crumbs for the lower
and middle class and there would have been

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:41.079
status quo center left foreign policy period,
a big picture.

00:03:41.079 --> 00:03:44.219
And Joe Biden is effectively the same as far
as that goes.

00:03:44.219 --> 00:03:49.840
We know what we get with him and in a sense
I think it's a good thing that this is now

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:50.840
out in the open.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:56.239
Uh, the contrast between Joe Biden and people
like Bernie Sanders and Elizabeth Warren is

00:03:56.239 --> 00:03:59.410
now much more clear, vote for what you want.

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:03.099
And it's now really clear what it is that
each candidate is offering.

00:04:03.099 --> 00:04:09.480
I actually, I've said before, I don't really
understand undecided voters two months or

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:15.370
a month before the election, once we've had
the debates and once we've had the primaries,

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:19.440
I really don't understand how someone could
be undecided at that point in time because

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:25.250
it's so clear how different whatever candidates
remain are at that point.

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:28.320
And even when you look at Hillary and Trump,
very, very different.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:32.780
I Know Hillary is a center left Democrat,
but very different than Donald Trump.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:35.990
And I didn't understand how someone could
be undecided a few weeks before the election

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:39.790
in 2016 as people would call in and tell me
that they were right.

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:43.410
Now I understand saying, you know, I'm on
the Progressive Wing.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:44.880
So for me it could be worn.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.960
It could be Bernie, it could be somebody else.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:50.630
If they end up being the nominee and if it's
Biden, I'm going to vote for him because he's

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:51.630
better than Trump.

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:52.630
Right?

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:56.820
Like it's super clear to me at this point,
sort of how someone might be in that mode.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:05:01.390
But what at this point is really great that
has come from these revelations from Joe Biden

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:06.180
and private, is that there is no more question
about what a Joe Biden presidency would be

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:11.300
if you had any question remaining, which many
of us who follow this stuff didn't safe for

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:13.160
very rich people.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:17.720
Crumbs for the lower and middle classes and
a center left foreign policy.

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:21.800
That's what we can expect and it's abundantly
clear and now we can all support the candidate

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:24.080
that we believe most aligns with our values.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:30.200
I want to hear from you, what do you make
of these statements by Joe Biden in private,

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:34.440
although we now know what was said, uh, to
very wealthy donors in New York City.

